  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-26: "Yes, start group C" (deferred-issue triage group C, notes/deferred-triage-2026-11.md). Read gh issue view 1767 and gh issue view 1663 (with the ebilling comment). Since PR #1756 (D-122) the evaluator computes spend/budget from FinanceBaseValues, while the matter/project form shows stored columns sprk_totalspendtodate, sprk_totalbudget, sprk_budgetutilizationpercent written only by FinanceRollupService (Services/Finance). Owner decision D-230: when the evaluator raises or updates a spend or budget Threshold Signal on a matter or project, it recalculates that one record's stored roll-up through the existing FinanceRollupService. First verify on origin/master d43fc9e16d how Threshold rules read spend today (#1663 says stored roll-ups; #1767 says computed): record the answer in the notes; if any Threshold rule still reads the stored columns, switch it to FinanceBaseValues in this task. ebilling-r1 owns FinanceRollupService and FinanceBaseValues: reuse them, do not fork; ask ebilling-r1 to review the PR (SendMessage to their session).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF, the ontology evaluator, the finance roll-up.</role>
  <goal>After a spend or budget Threshold Signal is raised or updated, the record's form shows the same figures the Signal states, with no mass or unchanged writes.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>D-61: never stamp unchanged rows; the recalculation runs only for the record whose Signal was raised or updated, and FinanceRollupService should skip the write when values are unchanged (check; add if missing, with ebilling's agreement). A recalculation fault must not fail Signal raising: log it. Which identity writes (the evaluator's writer UAMI vs the BFF) must match how FinanceRollupService writes today; do not add privileges without the owner.</background>
  </context>
  <constraints>
