  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A test fails on origin/master: raising (and updating) a spend Threshold Signal on a matter calls the roll-up recalculation for exactly that matter; same for a project.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Must-not-fire: a non-finance Signal, an unchanged Signal (no raise/update) and other records trigger no recalculation; a recalculation fault leaves the Signal raised and is logged; unchanged roll-up values are not rewritten.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Notes record how Threshold rules read spend on master; build, Signals and Finance filters, full ArchTests pass; publish-size delta reported; ebilling-r1 asked to review.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>The recalculation needs a new privilege, a schema change, a nightly or bulk write, or a change to FinanceRollupService's computation: STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <execution>
    <protocol>Run through task-execute. Fresh branch from origin/master in a short-path worktree (C:\wt232); PR to master; do not merge (the main session reviews and merges, D-115).</protocol>
